course: dictionary
lesson: 3599
title: Fiery: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «fiery» can mean more than one thing, so the context tells you which meaning you need. «The three friends were thrown into a fiery furnace but were not burnt.» A furnace is a very hot oven full of fire, so fiery means burning here.
explain: «A fiery sunset» and «fiery red hair» use fiery to mean bright red or orange, like flames. Ask what the word describes: a sunset is a sky, and hair is a colour, not a fire. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «A fiery temper» is about feelings, not heat. It describes someone who gets angry very fast. Food works the same way: «a fiery chilli» means very hot and spicy. Look at the word next to fiery to find its meaning.
fact: Fiery means burning or full of fire.
fact: Fiery can mean bright red or orange, like flames, as in «fiery red».
fact: Fiery can describe someone who is quick to get angry, as in «a fiery temper».
fact: Fiery can mean very hot and spicy, as in «a fiery chilli».
fact: In a Bible story, Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego were thrown into a fiery furnace and saved by God.
exercise: «The three friends were thrown into a fiery furnace.» What does fiery mean here? | *Burning, full of fire | Spicy and hot to eat | Bright and sunny | Angry and shouting
exercise: «A fiery temper» describes a person. What does fiery suggest? | Very spicy | Sleepy and calm | *Quick to get angry | Bright orange like a sunset
exercise: «A fiery curry» is served at dinner. What does fiery mean in this phrase? | Burning in a furnace | *Very hot and spicy | Bright red like a sky | Soft and sweet
test: Which meaning of fiery fits «fiery red hair»? | Pale grey | *Bright red or orange, like flames | Cold blue
test: Which phrase uses fiery to mean quick to get angry? | *a fiery temper | a fiery sunset | a fiery curry
exam: In «a fiery furnace», what does fiery mean? | *Burning, full of fire | Bright red like a sunset | Very spicy to eat | Quick to get angry
